    "body": "## Problem\r\nA hanging `:` stays after backspacing out of the command line.\r\n\r\n## Solution:\r\nClear the command line for empty commands. Note that `:<CR>` will now clear the command line too.\r\n\r\nCloses #40684 \r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-29T16:40:09Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Note that `:<CR>` will now clear the command line too.\r\n\r\nThat differs from Vim, but seems ok. Though TBH, I don't see what's wrong with showing the \":\" after backspace. \r\n\r\nIf anyone cares one way or another, leave a comment.",
